Nintendo's 3ds handheld family is deep  into its lifecycle and with so many  versions already released combined with  the high demand for the switch you may  be wondering where another 3ds model  fits in well with the new 2d s XL not  only will newcomers get access to its  vast library of games but we get the  best design version of this dedicated  handheld the original 2d s is an  entry-level version with its slate like  design and omission of audio  stereoscopic 3d now with the new 2d s XL  which retails for 150 bucks we have many  of the features that make the new 3ds XL  great larger screens stronger processor  and the c-stick and z LZ are buttons all  while being about two and a half ounces  lighter the new 2d s XL also adopts the  clamshell design of 3ds systems but  improved upon it it's slightly shorter  and a near-perfect seal is created  around the two halves when it's closed  this is due to how the two screens are  seated the bottom screen doesn't  protrude as with every other clamshell  based 3ds and the top screen has a sleek  smartphone like build the chassis sports  a matte finish which makes for better  grip and tops off the system simple  elegant look and every 3ds I've used the  hinge seems to feel a little loose  causing the top portion to wobble back  and forth if you gave it a little shake  unfortunately the same holds true for  the 2d s XL it's as if the top is  loosely screwed into the hinge this  gives a bit of a fragile feel to an  otherwise solidly built system as you  can tell from the name the 2d s XL  ditches the 3d capabilities but it isn't  essential to play any of the system's  games as it doesn't serve a gameplay  function since this is an XL model it's  equipped with a 3ds XL size displays a 4  point 9 inch screen up top and a 4.2  inch resistive touch screen on the  bottom both screens are well over an  inch bigger than those of the original  2d s however the 400 by 240 and the 320  by 240 resolutions feel somewhat  antiquated in 2017 they're noticeably  low res compared to many other devices  but you can exactly blame the new 2d s  XL high res screens would also require  Hardware faster than the already  upgraded processor of the new DS systems  like the other DS systems with the new  moniker the 2d SXL is equipped with the  quad-core arm 11 CPU at 804 megahertz  and does provide that extra juice for  snappier navigation through the  operating systems and UI there are a  handful of games that actually require  the faster hardware like xenoblade  chronicles binding of issac and a bunch  of SNES games on Virtual Console many  notable games run better and load faster  such as Pokemon Sun and Moon Monster  Hunter generations and Super Smash Bros  for 3ds so while the screens look  pixelated it doesn't negate the fact  that the platform is home to a breadth  of amazing games still haven't played  bravely default Fire Emblem awakening or  Zelda a link between worlds the time is  now the adoption of the c-stick means  you'll get superior camera controls and  additional functions in certain games  and while it looks and feel stiff the  c-stick accurately recognizes miniscule  movements the Circle Pad offers smooth  movement but it still doesn't match the  ergonomics of an actual analog stick  face buttons the d-pad and the triggers  all offer a solid tactile feel an NFC  reader is also built into the system so  you'll get support for all your amiibo  there are a few small changes compared  to the new 3ds XL the 2d s XL stereo  speakers are located at the bottom  corners of the body but at louder  volumes you'll notice that the sound  rattles the back end of the system which  makes it feel a little bit cheap the  front-facing camera is moved to the  hinge and the two forward facing cameras  move to the top of the backplate the  home button now sits below the d-pad and  the stylus is slightly shorter than the  previous three yes stylus along the  bottom of the system is the power button  and a 3.5 millimeter audio jack adjacent  to the stylus slot the enclosure that  houses the game cartridge and micro SD  card in particular is a noteworthy  improvement over the 3ds XL which how do  you take up a stubborn back place to  insert an SD card a 4 gigabyte Toshiba  micro SDHC card will already be inserted  with each new 2d s XL though you'll want  more storage capacity if you plan on  downloading your games one of the  biggest blunders of the new 3ds XL was  the absence of an AC adapter but don't  trip the new 2d s XL comes with the  charger when it comes to battery life  expect roughly three and a half to four  and a half hours of play time  I'm off a full charge I got  approximately three hours and 55 minutes  straight playing Zelda Ocarina of Time  with full brightness and Wi-Fi enabled  despite a few shortcomings there's a lot  to like about the new 2d SXL should you  consider buying one if you already have  a new 3ds XL probably not however if  you're still on one of the older DS  models or interested in jumping into the  expansive library of 3ds games I would  highly recommend you consider the new 2d  s XL the platform may be showing its age  but it's Nintendo's best vs system yet  are you thinking of getting a 2d s XL  tell us in the comments I know you liked  this video so give it a thumbs up and  subscribe to GameSpot for more tech and  game coverage thanks for watching
 

